      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 713969433,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1847260972,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795550556216,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Estimate a quantity by running many random\nexperiments and averaging the results.\n\nClassic example — estimating π:\n  · Throw N random darts at a unit square\n  · Count hits h inside the quarter-circle\n  · π  ≈  4 × h / N\n\nAs N grows, the estimate improves.\nError shrinks like 1/√N (see red box →)\n\nN = number of random samples thrown.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Estimate a quantity by running many random\nexperiments and averaging the results.\n\nClassic example — estimating π:\n  · Throw N random darts at a unit square\n  · Count hits h inside the quarter-circle\n  · π  ≈  4 × h / N\n\nAs N grows, the estimate improves.\nError shrinks like 1/√N (see red box →)\n\nN = number of random samples thrown.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
