    {
      "id": "qn014",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 620,
      "y": 192,
      "width": 402,
      "height": 245,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 904863220,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1870559932,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795550556216,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "N = the number of random samples\n    drawn in a simulation.\n\nDepends on context:\n  Estimating π    →  darts thrown\n  Coin flip LLN   →  number of flips\n  Option pricing  →  price paths run\n\nBigger N  →  smaller error,\n           but more compute time.\n\nThis trade-off is captured by:\n\n  error  ∝  1 / √N",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "N = the number of random samples\n    drawn in a simulation.\n\nDepends on context:\n  Estimating π    →  darts thrown\n  Coin flip LLN   →  number of flips\n  Option pricing  →  price paths run\n\nBigger N  →  smaller error,\n           but more compute time.\n\nThis trade-off is captured by:\n\n  error  ∝  1 / √N",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
