      "index": "w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 268273727,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 124850258,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795550556216,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Sample mean → true mean as n → ∞\n\nCoin flip (p = 0.5):\n  After 10 flips:   fraction ≈ 0.6\n  After 1,000:      fraction ≈ 0.51\n  After 10,000:     fraction ≈ 0.500x\n\nThe wobble shrinks like 1/√n.\n\nFoundation for all Monte Carlo:\n  \"run enough experiments and the\n   average will converge to the truth.\"\n\nBiased coin (p = 0.53):\n  Need ~1,000+ flips before the fraction\n  clearly separates from 0.5.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Sample mean → true mean as n → ∞\n\nCoin flip (p = 0.5):\n  After 10 flips:   fraction ≈ 0.6\n  After 1,000:      fraction ≈ 0.51\n  After 10,000:     fraction ≈ 0.500x\n\nThe wobble shrinks like 1/√n.\n\nFoundation for all Monte Carlo:\n  \"run enough experiments and the\n   average will converge to the truth.\"\n\nBiased coin (p = 0.53):\n  Need ~1,000+ flips before the fraction\n  clearly separates from 0.5.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
